,title,link,text,language,family
0,Leizhou Min - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leizhou_Min,"Leizhou or Luichew Min (simplified Chinese: 雷州话; traditional Chinese: 雷州話; pinyin: Léizhōuhuà, [le ɪʈʂo ʊ xwa]) is a branch of Min Chinese spoken in Leizhou city, Xuwen County, Mazhang District, most parts of Suixi County and also spoken inside of the linguistically diverse Xiashan District.","Chinese, Leizhou",Sino-Tibetan
1,The Sound of the Luichow Min language / dialect (UDHR ...TIAT-4-2-5-production12042025 - so06.tci-thaijo.orgLeizhou Min | 音楽と多言語Leizhou opera (雷剧) music compilation - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O8WT3G9RK8Y,"Aug 16, 2020 · In fact, many features of ancient Chinese retained in Luichow language. It was evolved from the ancient Quanzhang dialect brought by the Quanzhang immigrants’ community from Fujian Province.... The Leizhou Song was spread among the people of the Leizhou Peninsula and gradually improved over hundreds of years, forming a standardized structure and framework. Leizhou Song, an important folk song system in Guangdong, embodies the region's rich cultural heritage and distinct musical aesthetics. Sino-Tibetan languagesSinitic languagesChinese languageのLeizhou Minで歌われている音楽 (洋楽)のYouTube動画を掲載しています。 語族等、言語の分類も確認できます。 Nov 23, 2020 · Leizhou opera (雷剧) is an opera form originating from the Leizhou peninsula of Guangdong province, and is one of the four major opera forms of Guangdong.","Chinese, Leizhou",Sino-Tibetan
2,Leizhou Song_Baiduwiki - 百度百科,https://baike.baidu.com/en/item/Leizhou+Song/106511,"The Leizhou Song absorbed the vigorous style of the Han and Wei dynasties and was influenced by the poetic style of the High Tang period, possessing a strong earthy character. The antiphonal singing of Leizhou Song gave rise to the ""Girls' Song.""","Chinese, Leizhou",Sino-Tibetan
